<h2 id="about">What this tool does</h2>
<p>Extraction is deletion seen from the other side: instead of asking which pages to throw away, you tick the ones to keep, and the tool writes those into a fresh PDF in the order you selected. It is the fastest route from a 60-page annual report to the eight-page schedule your accountant asked for, or from one merged bundle of receipts to individual vendor files.</p>
<p>Every page of your document becomes a numbered button. Click them in any order — the selection list shows what you have picked so far, and you can also type a range such as 3-7,12 instead of tapping. Selected pages are copied with pdf-lib as real PDF objects, so text stays searchable, links stay clickable and the pages print exactly as they did in the source.</p>
<p>Because the whole job happens in the browser tab, a 400-page statement archive never touches a server: no upload wait, no privacy question, no watermark. When you press Download you get extract.pdf (renameable) containing only your chosen pages — the original file stays on your device unchanged.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-use">How to use the Extract PDF Pages <span style="color:var(--cy)">| Step by Step Guide</span></h2>
<div class="howto"><ol><li><span>Drop the source .pdf into the box; page buttons render as soon as the file is parsed locally.</span></li><li><span>Click the pages you want to keep, or type a range like 3-7,12 in the box and press Add.</span></li><li><span>Review the selection strip — it lists page numbers in the output order.</span></li><li><span>Press 'Create PDF' to build the new document (pdf-lib loads from the pinned CDN on this click).</span></li><li><span>Download the extracted file and rename it if you like before saving.</span></li></ol></div>
<span class="ru" data-ru lang="ros">PDF dalne ke baad har page number button ban jata hai. Jo pages nikal ke alag file banani hain un par click karein — ya range likhein jaise 3-7,12. 'Create PDF' dabayein aur sirf chune hue pages ki nayi file download karein. Sab kuch aapke browser me, koi upload nahi.</span>
<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
<ul class="feat-list"><li>Click-to-select page picker plus typed ranges (3-7,12 accepted)</li><li>Output follows your selection order — handy for reassembling slides</li><li>Real page copy: searchable text, live links, original fonts preserved</li><li>Instant page count and size estimate before you commit</li><li>Rename the result in the same step; default extract.pdf</li><li>No server: a 50-page extraction finishes in seconds on a normal laptop</li></ul>
<h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
<ul><li>Extract in one go rather than repeatedly if the file is large — every run re-reads the source.</li><li>For an entire chapter, checking the start and end page in a reader first avoids the classic off-by-one.</li><li>Need the extracted pages as pictures? Run PDF to Images on the small result — it is far quicker than rendering the big source.</li><li>Duplicate selections are ignored, so tapping page 7 twice does not produce two copies.</li><li>If the source is encrypted, extraction cannot read it; unlock once in a desktop reader, then extract here.</li></ul>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details><summary>Does extraction keep text selectable?</summary><p>Yes. Pages are copied as PDF objects, not converted to photos, so searching and copy-paste behave exactly like the original.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I extract the same page twice?</summary><p>Selections are unique — page 7 appears once no matter how often you tap it. To duplicate a page, extract it, then merge the small file with itself.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the extract pdf pages free to use?</summary><p>Yes — Extract PDF Pages has no usage cap, no sign-up and no watermark, and it is not a trial: the page is a static file on https://wafasmart.tech with no billing backend behind it. </p></details>
<details><summary>Does anything get uploaded when I use extract pdf pages?</summary><p>No. Extract PDF Pages reads your PDF straight into page memory, works on it locally and hands the result back as a download — there is no upload request to intercept, store or leak, and no log of what you processed.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between Extract and Delete?</summary><p>Extract keeps only what you pick; Delete removes what you pick and keeps the rest. Same engine, opposite selection — use whichever list is shorter.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use it on my phone?</summary><p>Yes. Extract PDF Pages is mobile-first: one column, big tap targets, and the system keyboard opens with sensible number/text input. On iPhone, Files and the share sheet feed the picker the same way Downloads does on Android. </p></details>
